# OPTIONAL. You do not need a .env file to run this project.
#
# docker-compose.yml already uses a dev-only default sa password (see the note at
# the top of that file for why it is committed). Create a .env only if you want a
# different password for your local container:
#
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env      # then uncomment and edit the line below
#
# If you change it:
#   1. Point the API at the same password without editing tracked files, e.g.
#      dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:QueueDb" "Server=127.0.0.1,1433;Database=QueueSystem;User Id=sa;Password=<new>;TrustServerCertificate=True" --project backend/src/QueueSystem.Api
#   2. SQL Server stores the sa password in its data volume on first start, so an
#      existing container keeps the old one. Recreate it with: docker compose down -v
#      (this deletes the local test data).
#
# SQL Server rule: at least 8 characters using 3 of upper case, lower case, digits and symbols.
# Do not use ; (it ends a connection string value) or $ (Docker Compose expands it).

# MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=Your-Own-Passw0rd!
